1
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:10,250
Sia: Pipsqueak!

2
00:00:11,840 --> 00:00:13,260
Sia: Stay out of my way!

3
00:00:13,590 --> 00:00:14,940
Sia: Or else!

4
00:01:46,220 --> 00:01:51,180
text: #02 THERE WAS A FORMIDABLE FOE
DEEP INSIDE THE DEN

5
00:02:00,850 --> 00:02:02,030
Sia: Not deep enough!

6
00:02:02,600 --> 00:02:04,030
Ario: Wow.

7
00:02:05,020 --> 00:02:06,590
Sia: You over there!

8
00:02:06,590 --> 00:02:09,660
Sia: If you can move, 
now's your chance to escape!

9
00:02:09,660 --> 00:02:11,330
Lock: Ario, Ginny, run for it!

10
00:02:11,330 --> 00:02:12,540
Ario: Y-Yeah!

11
00:02:11,330 --> 00:02:12,540
Ginny: Okay!

12
00:02:12,860 --> 00:02:13,910
Ario: Lock?!

13
00:02:13,910 --> 00:02:15,660
Lock: Watch for surprise goblin attacks.

14
00:02:17,660 --> 00:02:18,840
Ario: Let's go, Ginny!

15
00:02:18,840 --> 00:02:20,110
Ginny: R-Right!

16
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:24,200
Lock: You saw that you'd only 
get in the way here.

17
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:25,590
Lock: Well done, Ario.

18
00:02:28,720 --> 00:02:30,010
Lock: Want some help?

19
00:02:30,010 --> 00:02:32,920
Sia: Huh?! Didn't you run away?

20
00:02:32,920 --> 00:02:34,980
Lock: There's no need for me to run.

21
00:02:35,790 --> 00:02:37,960
Sia: Do what you want, then!

22
00:02:37,960 --> 00:02:40,910
Sia: But I don't need you jumping in!

23
00:02:44,610 --> 00:02:45,660
Lock: Hm...

24
00:02:48,950 --> 00:02:51,870
Lock: Say, you're currently losing.

25
00:02:51,870 --> 00:02:55,760
Sia: Are you saying I'm weaker 
than this underling?!

26
00:02:55,760 --> 00:02:58,530
Lock: No, I'm talking about your sword.

27
00:03:01,260 --> 00:03:02,640
Lock: See?

28
00:03:04,650 --> 00:03:06,270
Lock: You sure you don't want help?

29
00:03:06,270 --> 00:03:08,760
Sia: Just follow your friends, 
and get out of here!

30
00:03:21,130 --> 00:03:22,570
Lock: I'm done asking.

31
00:03:22,920 --> 00:03:24,700
Lock: I'll just take him down.

32
00:03:24,700 --> 00:03:25,780
Sia: You?!

33
00:03:35,770 --> 00:03:39,200
Lock: You... make too much noise.

34
00:03:44,700 --> 00:03:46,330
Lock: Were you hurt?

35
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:50,370
Sia: Who the hell...

36
00:03:50,370 --> 00:03:54,020
Sia: I mean, who are you, sir?

37
00:03:56,450 --> 00:03:58,240
Sia: Pardon me, sir.

38
00:03:58,240 --> 00:04:00,610
Sia: I am Sia, daughter of Danton, 

39
00:04:00,610 --> 00:04:03,160
Sia: the chieftain of
the Eastern Beastkin Tribe.

40
00:04:03,350 --> 00:04:07,650
Sia: I am grateful that you 
rescued me from danger.

41
00:04:07,970 --> 00:04:09,910
Sia: And you are?

42
00:04:11,690 --> 00:04:14,230
Lock: An F-rank adventurer who was passing by!

43
00:04:14,230 --> 00:04:16,160
Sia: You lie! Sir.

44
00:04:16,490 --> 00:04:17,480
Lock: Check it.

45
00:04:17,910 --> 00:04:20,670
Sia: Y-You really are F-rank?!

46
00:04:20,670 --> 00:04:22,230
Lock: I know, right?

47
00:04:22,230 --> 00:04:26,560
Sia: Why are you so proud 
of being F-rank, sir?

48
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:30,800
Sia: Besides, that strength 
was abnormal for an F-rank.

49
00:04:31,880 --> 00:04:33,640
Lock: It's a long story.

50
00:04:33,640 --> 00:04:34,940
Lock: What's your rank, Sia?

51
00:04:34,940 --> 00:04:37,120
Sia: I am B-rank, sir.

52
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:42,200
Sia: But now, it feels terribly rude for me 
to tell you to run away back there.

53
00:04:42,480 --> 00:04:45,190
Sia: I'm ashamed of myself, sir.

54
00:04:45,190 --> 00:04:48,940
Lock: You only did that because 
you thought I was a beginner.

55
00:04:48,940 --> 00:04:51,250
Sia: W-Well, yes, sir...

56
00:04:51,250 --> 00:04:54,080
Lock: For an adventurer, 
that was the right call.

57
00:04:55,020 --> 00:04:56,540
Lock: I'm Lock.

58
00:04:57,250 --> 00:04:59,960
Lock: A veteran F-rank adventurer.

59
00:04:59,960 --> 00:05:02,500
Sia: What does that even mean, sir?

60
00:05:02,840 --> 00:05:06,200
Lock: By the way, what lurks 
deeper inside here?

61
00:05:07,670 --> 00:05:12,200
Lock: Isn't there a much bigger fish here
 than a goblin lord?

62
00:05:13,100 --> 00:05:16,300
Sia: Wh-Whatever could you mean?

63
00:05:16,300 --> 00:05:20,450
Lock: Earlier, you called the 
goblin lord an underling.

64
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:23,500
Lock: That means there's a stronger enemy.

65
00:05:23,500 --> 00:05:25,370
Sia: Well, I mean...

66
00:05:25,370 --> 00:05:27,200
Lock: You don't have to tell me 
if you don't want to.

67
00:05:27,620 --> 00:05:30,130
Sia: Hey! Where are you going, sir?!

68
00:05:30,130 --> 00:05:32,910
Lock: I was contracted to exterminate goblins.

69
00:05:33,320 --> 00:05:35,600
Lock: But if there's a bigger threat than that, 

70
00:05:35,600 --> 00:05:38,750
Lock: I have to keep going for the sake 
of nearby villages.

71
00:05:39,090 --> 00:05:40,580
Lock: And I'll defeat it.

72
00:05:40,580 --> 00:05:43,880
Sia: This won't be a foe 
that's so easy to defeat, sir.

73
00:05:43,880 --> 00:05:47,380
Sia: We're up against... a vampire lord!

74
00:05:47,380 --> 00:05:50,500
Lock: Aha, a vampire lord.

75
00:05:50,500 --> 00:05:55,390
Lock: Abnormally high vitality. 
Transforms into bats, or mist.

76
00:05:55,800 --> 00:05:58,390
Lock: That's a troublesome opponent indeed.

77
00:05:58,860 --> 00:06:00,830
Lock: Isn't that a lot for you to handle, Sia?

78
00:06:00,830 --> 00:06:02,770
Sia: Wh-Why is that, sir?

79
00:06:02,770 --> 00:06:05,700
Lock: Well, a mere goblin lord gave you trouble.

80
00:06:06,810 --> 00:06:12,040
Sia: Even so, sir, I can't afford to run away!

81
00:06:12,040 --> 00:06:14,400
Lock: Fine, but don't get hurt.

82
00:06:14,770 --> 00:06:17,300
Sia: You aren't going to ask why?

83
00:06:17,300 --> 00:06:19,070
Lock: Do you want me to ask?

84
00:06:19,070 --> 00:06:20,230
Sia: No.

85
00:06:20,230 --> 00:06:21,620
Lock: Then I won't.

86
00:06:22,740 --> 00:06:27,570
Sia: Our tribe has hunted 
vampires for generations.

87
00:06:27,570 --> 00:06:29,000
Lock: She's telling me anyway?

88
00:06:29,290 --> 00:06:32,780
Sia: A while ago, we were fighting vampires, 

89
00:06:32,780 --> 00:06:35,790
Sia: and we had them down to just one.

90
00:06:35,790 --> 00:06:38,440
Sia: But after my father, the chieftain, 
 was badly wounded, 

91
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:40,810
Sia: we ended up letting it get away.

92
00:06:41,170 --> 00:06:42,840
Sia: That one escapee...

93
00:06:42,840 --> 00:06:46,310
Lock: ...was, of all things, a vampire lord.

94
00:06:46,830 --> 00:06:50,640
Sia: It was my tribe's failure 
that it escaped, sir.

95
00:06:50,640 --> 00:06:56,830
Sia: It's my duty as chieftain's daughter 
to restore my tribe's honor!

96
00:06:57,070 --> 00:06:59,110
Sia: I've been pursuing him for months, 

97
00:06:59,110 --> 00:07:01,820
Sia: and now I finally know where he is!

98
00:07:02,570 --> 00:07:04,970
Lock: Is it against the rules for someone

99
00:07:04,970 --> 00:07:07,840
Lock: to help you beat him 
and restore your tribe's honor?

100
00:07:07,840 --> 00:07:12,880
Sia: No, sir. It will be restored 
even if I receive help.

101
00:07:12,880 --> 00:07:14,240
Lock: Good, then.

102
00:07:14,240 --> 00:07:17,850
Sia: But I still think 
you should go back, Lock.

103
00:07:19,350 --> 00:07:21,770
Lock: You can't fight without a weapon.

104
00:07:21,770 --> 00:07:23,100
Lock: I'll let you borrow this.

105
00:07:23,100 --> 00:07:26,480
Sia: Huh? Th-Then what will you use?

106
00:07:26,790 --> 00:07:28,670
Lock: I'm powerful even barehanded!

107
00:07:30,640 --> 00:07:32,720
Sia: Thank you, sir.

108
00:07:33,250 --> 00:07:37,910
Sia: He's telling me to be the one to 
strike down the vampire lord.

109
00:07:37,910 --> 00:07:40,870
Sia: That's why he's bluffing 
about fighting barehanded.

110
00:07:51,860 --> 00:07:53,930
Lock: Looks like that's the end of them.

111
00:07:53,930 --> 00:07:57,510
Sia: Y-You really are strong 
even unarmed, sir!

112
00:07:57,510 --> 00:07:59,130
Lock: Aren't I?

113
00:07:59,130 --> 00:08:02,270
Lock: Well, I'm originally a sorcerer.

114
00:08:02,270 --> 00:08:06,200
Lock: I used to be with Eric and Goran, 
who were abnormally strong, 

115
00:08:06,200 --> 00:08:11,280
Lock: so I was stuck firing off magic from 
the rear, but I was still S-rank.

116
00:08:11,830 --> 00:08:16,900
Lock: Also, I spent ten years fighting 
a demon horde and the Demon King, 

117
00:08:16,900 --> 00:08:19,850
Lock: so my martial arts 
improved in a mad hurry.

118
00:08:20,670 --> 00:08:23,240
Lock: Well, what say we attack 
that throne room?

119
00:08:23,240 --> 00:08:25,290
Sia: Y-Yes, sir!

120
00:08:30,050 --> 00:08:35,929
Vampire Lord: Hmph. So the little puppy girl 
tries to reach above her station.

121
00:08:35,929 --> 00:08:37,330
Sia: You shut up!

122
00:08:37,330 --> 00:08:39,679
Sia: You're cornered now, vampire lord!

123
00:08:39,679 --> 00:08:42,940
Sia: I swear I'll take you down myself!

124
00:08:44,130 --> 00:08:50,190
Vampire Lord: When it took all your father 
could muster to even scratch me?

125
00:08:50,190 --> 00:08:54,120
Vampire Lord: You, defeat me? 
When you're weaker than him?

126
00:08:54,840 --> 00:08:57,200
Vampire Lord: Don't be ridiculous.

127
00:08:59,410 --> 00:09:01,950
Vampire Lord: Think again, girl.

128
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:07,270
Vampire Lord: For baring your fangs at me, 
the lord of the night, 

129
00:09:07,270 --> 00:09:10,710
Vampire Lord: regret will be the last feeling 
you ever have!

130
00:09:10,710 --> 00:09:12,740
Lock: I get it now.

131
00:09:12,740 --> 00:09:15,730
Lock: You must have been making 
the goblin pack look small

132
00:09:15,730 --> 00:09:18,220
Lock: so you could lure adventures down here.

133
00:09:18,490 --> 00:09:22,370
Vampire Lord: Well, well. You're apparently 
not a complete fool.

134
00:09:22,370 --> 00:09:25,050
Vampire Lord: You qualify to be my servant.

135
00:09:25,050 --> 00:09:30,290
Vampire Lord: But puppy, I must commend you 
for bringing a human along.

136
00:09:30,290 --> 00:09:31,230
Sia: Huh?

137
00:09:31,230 --> 00:09:35,080
Sia: My Vampiric Charm 
won't work on a mere beast.

138
00:09:35,080 --> 00:09:38,990
Sia: But I can use it to turn 
a human into my servant.

139
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:41,870
Sia: Oh no!

140
00:09:41,870 --> 00:09:43,900
Sia: Lock, run for it!

141
00:09:43,900 --> 00:09:45,800
Vampire Lord: It's too late!

142
00:09:53,470 --> 00:09:55,230
Sia: L-Lock...

143
00:09:55,230 --> 00:09:56,460
Vampire Lord: Come here.

144
00:10:02,980 --> 00:10:06,110
Sia: This was entirely my mistake.

145
00:10:06,110 --> 00:10:07,600
Vampire Lord: Dog girl.

146
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:13,350
Vampire Lord: Choose. Will you die by my hand, or his?

147
00:10:22,870 --> 00:10:24,040
Sia: Huh?

148
00:10:24,870 --> 00:10:28,370
Vampire Lord: N-No! Why didn't it work?!

149
00:10:28,370 --> 00:10:32,010
Lock: Because I have a high resistance 
to mental debuffs.

150
00:10:32,010 --> 00:10:33,580
Vampire Lord: Get real!

151
00:10:33,580 --> 00:10:36,550
Vampire Lord: A mere human could never withstand 
a vampire lord's Vampiric Charm!

152
00:10:36,550 --> 00:10:40,270
Lock: Then you must not be a vampire lord.

153
00:10:40,800 --> 00:10:46,730
Lock: Maybe you're a lesser vampire 
who's convinced he's a vampire lord.

154
00:10:46,730 --> 00:10:49,850
Sia: H-He sure is poking the bear.

155
00:10:50,440 --> 00:10:52,690
Vampire Lord: H-How dare you?!

156
00:10:52,690 --> 00:10:53,610
Sia: Look out!

157
00:10:57,190 --> 00:11:01,000
Lock: You're darn quick for a lesser vampire.

158
00:11:01,370 --> 00:11:03,250
Vampire Lord: You'll pay...

159
00:11:03,250 --> 00:11:06,440
Vampire Lord: You shall pay dearly!

160
00:11:06,790 --> 00:11:10,540
Vampire Lord: You'll rue the day you mocked me!

161
00:11:12,390 --> 00:11:15,050
Sia: That's... a high-level magic circle!

162
00:11:15,050 --> 00:11:16,670
Lock: Super Speed.

163
00:11:17,920 --> 00:11:19,680
Lock: Drain Touch!

164
00:11:19,680 --> 00:11:21,680
Vampire Lord: Th-This spell is...!

165
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:24,500
Lock: You're good at absorbing life force, 

166
00:11:24,500 --> 00:11:27,810
Lock: but not at having it taken 
from you, lesser vampire!

167
00:11:35,670 --> 00:11:39,570
Vampire Lord: Who the hell are you?

168
00:11:39,850 --> 00:11:42,120
Lock: Lock, the F-rank adventurer.

169
00:11:42,120 --> 00:11:43,560
Vampire Lord: Stop messing with me!

170
00:11:44,530 --> 00:11:46,180
Vampire Lord: Fine, then.

171
00:11:46,570 --> 00:11:50,980
Vampire Lord: But don't forget, 
you have provoked my wrath!

172
00:11:50,980 --> 00:11:54,630
Vampire Lord: Never again will you 
spend a peaceful night!

173
00:11:55,780 --> 00:11:58,000
Lock: Typical bloodsucker bluster.

174
00:11:58,420 --> 00:12:00,420
Sia: You won't escape!

175
00:12:02,930 --> 00:12:06,210
Vampire Lord: Wha?! I-I can't regenerate!

176
00:12:09,300 --> 00:12:16,110
Vampire Lord: By destroying me... 
the medallion's already...

177
00:12:17,060 --> 00:12:19,090
Lock: Looks like that came in handy.

178
00:12:19,090 --> 00:12:20,810
Sia: Thank you, sir.

179
00:12:20,810 --> 00:12:22,700
Sia: The blade is so sharp.

180
00:12:23,020 --> 00:12:27,620
Sia: And I felt some kind of power 
well up when I sliced him.

181
00:12:27,620 --> 00:12:30,320
Lock: Y-You must have imagined it.

182
00:12:30,320 --> 00:12:33,620
Lock: I can't tell her it's 
the Demon King's sword.

183
00:12:34,450 --> 00:12:35,860
Lock: What're you doing?

184
00:12:35,860 --> 00:12:37,880
Sia: Oh! Found it, sir!

185
00:12:38,870 --> 00:12:40,130
Lock: What is it?

186
00:12:40,130 --> 00:12:45,380
Sia: A cursed medallion, found inside 
the bodies of special vampire lords.

187
00:12:45,380 --> 00:12:46,910
Lock: Cursed medallion?

188
00:12:47,630 --> 00:12:53,270
Sia: When a vampire lord with one of these 
inside sucks blood or kills someone, 

189
00:12:53,270 --> 00:12:55,560
Sia: a curse builds up in the medallion.

190
00:12:55,900 --> 00:12:58,590
Lock: These weren't around ten years ago.

191
00:12:58,590 --> 00:13:01,100
Lock: Are they a new fad with vampires?

192
00:13:02,660 --> 00:13:07,290
Vampire Lord: Defeating me will bring you no peace!

193
00:13:07,290 --> 00:13:12,040
Vampire Lord: The medallion's power will soon open 
a portal to the dimensional rift!

194
00:13:12,040 --> 00:13:13,910
Lock: Dimensional rift?

195
00:13:13,910 --> 00:13:15,620
Vampire Lord: That's right.

196
00:13:15,620 --> 00:13:20,600
Vampire Lord: Once the portal opens, countless demons 
will surge forth and overrun this world.

197
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:27,060
Vampire Lord: And from the other dimension 
shall come our dark gods!

198
00:13:27,060 --> 00:13:29,680
Sia: Dark gods?

199
00:13:29,680 --> 00:13:31,650
Lock: The dimensional rift.

200
00:13:31,650 --> 00:13:35,910
Lock: That's where, until recently, 
I'd been fighting for ten years.

201
00:13:36,340 --> 00:13:40,090
Lock: We don't know how to open 
a portal to it from this side.

202
00:13:41,250 --> 00:13:45,530
Lock: A decade ago, we fought 
the Demon King on our side, 

203
00:13:45,530 --> 00:13:47,970
Lock: and when he fled into 
the dimensional rift, 

204
00:13:47,970 --> 00:13:50,540
Lock: we leaped in before the portal closed.

205
00:13:50,540 --> 00:13:52,430
Lock: It's usually an exit-only affair.

206
00:13:52,970 --> 00:13:58,730
Lock: That's why Eric and Goran were unable 
to come help me once they'd left.

207
00:13:58,730 --> 00:14:04,020
Vampire Lord: Live in terror until 
the advent of the dark gods!

208
00:14:04,020 --> 00:14:09,600
Vampire Lord: Many vampire lords will be drawn to that 
medallion, and eventually one will—

209
00:14:17,800 --> 00:14:21,760
Vampire Lord: Y-You absorbed the curse?!

210
00:14:22,750 --> 00:14:26,850
Lock: Even if a dimensional portal 
does open, no demons will come.

211
00:14:28,720 --> 00:14:31,370
Lock: Because I already kicked all their asses.

212
00:14:32,710 --> 00:14:34,560
Vampire Lord: That sword...

213
00:14:34,560 --> 00:14:37,460
Vampire Lord: The Demon King's sword...

214
00:14:37,460 --> 00:14:40,730
Vampire Lord: You... You couldn't be...

215
00:14:40,730 --> 00:14:42,210
Vampire Lord: the Great Sage Lu—

216
00:14:50,410 --> 00:14:55,100
Sia: L-Luck? Great Sage Luck?

217
00:14:55,730 --> 00:14:58,860
Lock: Sorry I cut up the medallion.

218
00:14:58,860 --> 00:15:03,540
Sia: Oh, no problem if it's 
in two pieces, sir.

219
00:15:05,610 --> 00:15:08,860
Lock: Ario and Ginny are probably 
worried, so let's hurry.

220
00:15:09,240 --> 00:15:13,860
Sia: Are you sure those two 
are all right, Luck?

221
00:15:14,130 --> 00:15:18,360
Lock: They're fine. 
They're both great, for F-ranks.

222
00:15:21,260 --> 00:15:26,940
Sia: I said "Luck" when I asked 
you just now, not "Lock."

223
00:15:30,960 --> 00:15:35,560
Sia: Sir, are you the Great Saint Luck?

224
00:15:40,120 --> 00:15:42,060
Lock: It's a secret.

225
00:15:42,890 --> 00:15:46,940
Sia: Yes, sir! 
I will guard your secret with my life!

226
00:15:46,940 --> 00:15:50,060
Lock: No need to be that determined.

227
00:15:50,060 --> 00:15:51,710
Sia: Now that I look again, 

228
00:15:51,710 --> 00:15:55,800
Sia: you do look like 
Great Saint Luck's statue.

229
00:15:55,800 --> 00:15:58,950
Lock: Huh? No, I don't!

230
00:16:04,230 --> 00:16:06,080
Lock: Goblin gems.

231
00:16:06,410 --> 00:16:09,390
Arone: It's good to see you safe and sound...

232
00:16:09,390 --> 00:16:11,330
Arone: but how did you get so many?!

233
00:16:11,330 --> 00:16:13,990
Ginny: The pack was bigger than expected.

234
00:16:13,990 --> 00:16:17,980
Ario: Sia the B-rank adventurer happened to 
be there to help us exterminate them.

235
00:16:19,710 --> 00:16:22,060
Arone: The guild should have 
assessed this job more accurately.

236
00:16:22,540 --> 00:16:24,630
Arone: We apologize!

237
00:16:25,510 --> 00:16:28,550
Sia: Looks like the guild's 
going to do something

238
00:16:28,550 --> 00:16:30,600
Sia: about the vampire lord incident, too.

239
00:16:30,600 --> 00:16:31,750
Lock: Okay.

240
00:16:34,290 --> 00:16:35,860
Lock: What're you doing?

241
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:40,360
Ario: Oh, Lock. You should thank 
Great Sage Luck, too.

242
00:16:40,820 --> 00:16:44,690
Ario: His protection was part of why 
we safely completed this job.

243
00:16:44,690 --> 00:16:48,630
Ginny: He's also the one who gave us 
this time of peace.

244
00:16:48,630 --> 00:16:51,630
text: HEE HEE

245
00:16:51,870 --> 00:16:53,000
Ario: See ya, Lock.

246
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:55,370
Ginny: Let's team up again if we get the chance.

247
00:16:55,370 --> 00:16:56,350
Lock: Sure.

248
00:16:59,820 --> 00:17:03,400
Sia: Thank you again, Lock.

249
00:17:03,400 --> 00:17:06,619
Sia: Now I can redeem my tribe's honor.

250
00:17:08,140 --> 00:17:10,599
Lock: Hey, quit thanking me.

251
00:17:10,970 --> 00:17:12,020
Lock: By the way, 

252
00:17:12,020 --> 00:17:17,030
Lock: would you mind sharing
 the vampire info your tribe learns?

253
00:17:17,030 --> 00:17:18,790
Sia: No problem, sir!

254
00:17:19,160 --> 00:17:24,319
Lock: I'm not about to let the peace we've 
defended for ten years just come undone!

255
00:17:24,780 --> 00:17:25,829
Sia: Stare.

256
00:17:26,210 --> 00:17:27,170
Lock: What?

257
00:17:27,170 --> 00:17:30,590
Sia: I told you, Lock. 
You do look like the Luck statue.

258
00:17:30,590 --> 00:17:33,460
Lock: Enough of that, already.

259
00:17:33,460 --> 00:17:35,720
Sia: Understood, sir.

260
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:40,960
Sia: You can speak directly with 
Lord Morton, can't you?

261
00:17:40,960 --> 00:17:42,580
Lock: Lord Morton?

262
00:17:42,580 --> 00:17:44,470
Lock: Oh, you mean Goran.

263
00:17:44,470 --> 00:17:50,480
Sia: I'd like you to urge Lord Morton 
to be on the look out for vampire lords.

264
00:17:50,480 --> 00:17:52,570
Lock: Didn't you report it to the guild?

265
00:17:52,570 --> 00:17:53,590
Sia: Yes, sir.

266
00:17:53,590 --> 00:17:56,300
Sia: But it's possible it'll be too late

267
00:17:56,300 --> 00:18:00,870
Sia: once they verify the story 
and relay it to the guildmaster.

268
00:18:01,780 --> 00:18:03,830
Lock: I follow.

269
00:18:03,830 --> 00:18:04,830
Sia: Lock.

270
00:18:05,380 --> 00:18:06,620
Sia: Take this.

271
00:18:08,040 --> 00:18:09,250
Lock: You sure?

272
00:18:09,250 --> 00:18:12,470
Sia: I'm fine having just half of it, 

273
00:18:12,470 --> 00:18:17,140
Sia: and wouldn't it be best to have proof 
when you explain to Lord Morton?

274
00:18:17,140 --> 00:18:19,630
Lock: Okay. I'll hang on to it.

275
00:18:20,890 --> 00:18:22,040
Sia: Right, sir!

276
00:18:22,040 --> 00:18:25,900
Sia: I'll go straight back to my 
village and gather information!

277
00:18:26,630 --> 00:18:27,730
Lock: Sure!

278
00:18:28,880 --> 00:18:32,050
Lock: Guess I'll go bring Goran up to speed.

279
00:18:32,780 --> 00:18:34,820
Goran: What gives?!

280
00:18:34,820 --> 00:18:37,510
Goran: Who says they're going out for "a bit" 
and comes back three days later?!

281
00:18:37,510 --> 00:18:38,820
Goran: Of course I'd worry!

282
00:18:38,820 --> 00:18:41,690
Lock: Hey, it was just three days.

283
00:18:41,690 --> 00:18:44,200
Goran: Just three days, but three whole days.

284
00:18:44,430 --> 00:18:47,620
Goran: If you're gonna be out late, 
drop me a line about it first!

285
00:18:47,620 --> 00:18:49,700
Lock: Who are you, my mother?

286
00:18:49,960 --> 00:18:52,960
Lock: Listen, something important has come up.

287
00:18:53,280 --> 00:18:55,150
Goran: What's that medallion?

288
00:18:55,720 --> 00:18:58,220
Lock: We could be in some trouble.

289
00:19:01,240 --> 00:19:03,340
Goran: That's what they're planning?

290
00:19:03,750 --> 00:19:07,210
Lock: Who'd have thought the demons 
and even the Demon King

291
00:19:07,210 --> 00:19:10,600
Lock: were just a vanguard for the dark gods.

292
00:19:11,970 --> 00:19:15,510
Goran: I'd like to have a specialized agency 
investigate this medallion.

293
00:19:15,510 --> 00:19:16,730
Goran: Mind if I borrow it?

294
00:19:16,730 --> 00:19:18,740
Lock: Sure, go for it.

295
00:19:18,740 --> 00:19:21,410
Goran: Wonder what it's made of.

296
00:19:21,410 --> 00:19:24,500
Lock: It looks like gold, but it isn't.

297
00:19:24,500 --> 00:19:27,930
Goran: Doesn't seem to be orichalcum 
or mithril, either.

298
00:19:27,930 --> 00:19:30,000
Goran: Even you can't tell, as a sorcerer?

299
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:31,900
Lock: Unfortunately, no.

300
00:19:31,900 --> 00:19:34,260
Lock: Maybe an alchemist could figure it out.

301
00:19:35,720 --> 00:19:36,840
Lock: Well.

302
00:19:37,250 --> 00:19:39,020
Lock: Time for me to get some sleep.

303
00:19:39,740 --> 00:19:40,720
Goran: Lock.

304
00:19:40,720 --> 00:19:41,240
Lock: Huh?

305
00:19:41,240 --> 00:19:44,420
Goran: Thank you for protecting 
those rookie adventurers.

306
00:19:45,400 --> 00:19:47,880
Goran: I mean that as guildmaster.

307
00:19:48,580 --> 00:19:50,250
Lock: Think nothin' of it.

308
00:19:50,250 --> 00:19:51,760
Lock: Good night.

309
00:19:54,540 --> 00:19:56,170
Lock: Yow!

310
00:19:56,710 --> 00:20:00,350
Goran: Celliss, good timing. 
I'd like to introd—

311
00:20:02,090 --> 00:20:03,280
Lock: Who's she?

312
00:20:03,280 --> 00:20:06,540
Goran: My daughter Celliss. 
She's almost fifteen.

313
00:20:06,540 --> 00:20:11,720
Lock: Ah! The one you said might have forgotten 
what you look like, back in the rift.

314
00:20:11,720 --> 00:20:13,910
Lock: Does she not like me or something?

315
00:20:13,910 --> 00:20:16,430
Goran: No, she's avoiding me.

316
00:20:16,430 --> 00:20:19,920
Goran: I was against her desire 
to become an adventurer.

317
00:20:20,250 --> 00:20:22,040
Lock: Why're you against it?

318
00:20:22,040 --> 00:20:25,770
Goran: Parental bias aside, the fact is, 
she's got B-rank ability.

319
00:20:25,770 --> 00:20:26,800
Lock: Why, then?

320
00:20:26,800 --> 00:20:28,790
Goran: But she's still a child.

321
00:20:28,790 --> 00:20:32,770
Goran: She lacks the insight and 
wariness an adventurer needs.

322
00:20:32,770 --> 00:20:35,940
Lock: Don't you get those through experience?

323
00:20:35,940 --> 00:20:38,690
Goran: I'd like to get my wife's input on this, 

324
00:20:38,690 --> 00:20:40,720
Goran: but she's on a trip
to a neighboring country.

325
00:20:40,720 --> 00:20:44,830
Lock: Oh, okay. I guess
 being a father's not easy.

326
00:20:45,440 --> 00:20:47,920
Goran: Lock, I need a favor.

327
00:20:59,750 --> 00:21:03,070
Lock: She definitely did inherit 
her dad's talent.

328
00:21:04,980 --> 00:21:07,080
Goran: Once Celliss is fifteen, 

329
00:21:07,460 --> 00:21:10,800
Goran: she won't need parental consent 
to register as an adventurer.

330
00:21:10,800 --> 00:21:15,550
Goran: At this rate, she might just go do so, 
and then start adventuring.

331
00:21:16,060 --> 00:21:20,260
Goran: When the time comes, could you 
casually keep an eye on her?

332
00:21:22,230 --> 00:21:24,330
Lock: Keep an eye on her?

333
00:21:27,360 --> 00:21:30,490
Lock: She's the one glaring holes into me.

334
00:21:39,810 --> 00:21:43,510
maid: Lady Celliss, 
how much bread would you like?

335
00:21:44,310 --> 00:21:46,000
Celliss: Three pieces, please.

336
00:21:49,990 --> 00:21:52,630
Lock: Uh, can I help you?

337
00:21:53,770 --> 00:21:55,040
Celliss: You...

338
00:21:58,220 --> 00:22:00,150
Celliss: You're Papa's illegitimate child, 
aren't you?!

339
00:22:05,030 --> 00:22:06,530
Credits: TRANSLATION: DUANE JOHNSON

340
00:22:06,530 --> 00:22:08,280
Credits: TIMING: EDGAR CRUZ
EDITING: ZACHARY CARLYSLE

341
00:22:08,280 --> 00:22:10,240
Credits: QUALITY CONTROL: GABRIELLA ALABANZA
TRANSLATION CHECK: SRIRAM GURUNATHAN

342
00:23:34,990 --> 00:23:40,070
text (top): NEXT TIME: SHE SUSPECTS I'M HER BASTARD BROTHER, 
AND NOW WE'RE GOING ON HER FIRST ADVENTURE
